class_name Tracks
extends RefCounted
## The six tracks, one per leg of the multiversal Grand Prix, in race order: out of the city of
## invention at nightfall, through its countryside, over a portal to the green banks of a revived
## desert river, onto the elevated track above a primordial jungle, back across the boiling desert,
## and home for the finale in the heart of the city.
##
## layout: the lap as driven from the start line, heading +x: ["S", metres] straight, ["L"/"R",
##   radius, degrees] a bend. Turns add up to 360 degrees; any small gap at the end is spread over
##   the lap. Check a layout with `python3 tools/track_check.py` (length, bends, clearances, map).
## heights: [fraction of the lap, road height in metres], eased between.
## indoor: [style, from, to] stretches (fractions of the lap) under a roof, with their own light
##   (Track.INDOOR); events never start in them.
## Landmarks: [kind, where along the lap (0..1), side (-1 left, 1 right), metres from the road, scale].
## events: the two world-event kinds (Hazards.KINDS) that can strike during a race here.

